# Trivy misconfiguration allowlist for the security.yml trivy-fs lane.
#
# DS-0002 ("Image user should not be 'root'") — accepted for
# .devcontainer/Dockerfile only. Verified 2026-09-15: `trivy fs .` over the
# full repo currently reports exactly one DS-0002 finding, in that file;
# every deployed image (backend, frontend-web, frontend-admin,
# mobile-app/reactnative, mobile-app/reactnative/backend) already sets a
# non-root USER. .devcontainer/Dockerfile's own header already explains why
# it's a false positive there (devcontainer.json sets "remoteUser": "vscode";
# the toolchain FEATURES that layer onto this image need root at build time)
# and carries a `# trivy:ignore:DS-0002` comment — but that inline form does
# not suppress this specific check (confirmed empirically: it has no effect
# regardless of placement, tested at the top of the file, directly above
# FROM, and as the very last line, with both `DS-0002` and `AVD-DS-0002`
# spellings — likely because DS-0002 reports against the image as a whole
# rather than a single instruction, so it has no AST node for a Dockerfile
# inline comment to attach to). This
# file's default-discovery (`--ignorefile` defaults to ".trivyignore" at cwd,
# and `trivy fs .` runs from the repo root) is the actual suppression
# mechanism. If a future Dockerfile is added without a USER directive, this
# entry will ALSO silence its finding — re-verify per-file before assuming
# it's still only .devcontainer/Dockerfile affected.
DS-0002

# DS-0026 ("No HEALTHCHECK defined") — accepted for
# .devcontainer/Dockerfile (interactively opened dev image; no orchestrator
# ever polls it) and mobile-app/reactnative/backend/Dockerfile (distroless:
# no shell, so HEALTHCHECK CMD cannot run; the service exposes /healthz and
# is probed by the orchestrator instead). Same scoping caveat as DS-0002:
# .trivyignore cannot scope a rule to a path, so a future Dockerfile without
# a HEALTHCHECK is also silenced — re-verify before assuming the set is
# still only these two. Re-verified 2026-10-02 on trivy v0.70.0 (the CI-pinned
# version): DS-0026 reports at file scope (startLine 1, no instruction node),
# so the inline `# trivy:ignore:DS-0026` comments both files used to carry do
# NOT suppress it under trivy >= 0.70 — the earlier comment below claiming
# otherwise was validated on an older trivy and is wrong now.
DS-0026

# -- Vulnerabilities ------------------------------------------------------
# CVE-2025-71329 / CVE-2025-71330 — HIGH DoS in image-size@1.2.1, reached
# only as a transitive dependency of metro (metro -> image-size@^1.0.2) in
# mobile-app/reactnative/package-lock.json. image-size runs at bundle/build
# time on the app's own checked-in assets, never on attacker-controlled
# input, so the crafted-ICNS crash vector is not reachable in production.
# The fix (image-size@2.x) is a major bump metro's range does not accept and
# metro@latest has dropped the dependency entirely — the override path
# resolves on the next react-native/metro upgrade rather than forcing an
# incompatible metro bump in this repo.
CVE-2025-71329
CVE-2025-71330
